---

# 🧩 PART 1 — DIMDIAMETER

---

# 🧠 1. Purpose

`DIMDIAMETER` measures circle/arc diameter using:

```text id="8d3jcv"
leader line
+
arrow
+
diameter symbol prefix (⌀)
+
dimension text
```

---

# 🚀 CAD Behavior

Depending on available space:

| Case         | Behavior              |
| ------------ | --------------------- |
| Large circle | text inside           |
| Small circle | text outside + leader |

---

# 📦 2. Semantic Data Model

```pseudo id="wd7xul"
DiameterDimension {

  targetEntityId

  center
  radius

  pickPoint

  textPosition?     // optional override

  styleId

  userTextOverride?
}
```

---

# 🚀 IMPORTANT

Do NOT store final geometry.

Store semantic intent only.

---

# ⚙️ 3. Main Pipeline

```pseudo id="sbcgpi"
FUNCTION buildDiameterDimension(dim):

  solveAnchor()

  solveLeader()

  solveArrow()

  solveText()

  buildRenderData()

  RETURN renderData
```

---

# 📐 4. Solve Diameter Direction

---

# STEP 1 — Vector From Center

```pseudo id="4k1k25"
v = NORMALIZE(
    pickPoint - center
)
```

This determines:

* leader direction
* arrow direction
* text side

---

# STEP 2 — Circle Edge Point

```pseudo id="rk0n6o"
edgePoint =
    center + v * radius
```

---

# STEP 3 — Opposite Point

```pseudo id="yjlwmk"
oppositePoint =
    center - v * radius
```

---

# 🚀 These define actual diameter axis.

---

# 📏 5. Measurement

```pseudo id="nt1x2j"
diameter = radius * 2
```

---

# 🔠 6. Format Text

---

# Default Text

```pseudo id="ezn0mq"
text =
    "⌀" +
    formatUnits(diameter)
```

---

# User Override

```pseudo id="38mm1u"
IF userTextOverride EXISTS:
    text = userTextOverride
```

---

# 🏹 7. Arrow Solver

---

# Arrow Always Points Toward Center

```pseudo id="nq9i8v"
arrow.position = edgePoint

arrow.direction = -v
```

---

# Pixel-Space Size

```pseudo id="mjlwm2"
arrowSizeWorld =
    pixelsToWorld(
        style.arrowSizePx
    )
```

---

# Build Geometry

```pseudo id="ys4rx4"
arrow =
    buildArrow(
        edgePoint,
        -v,
        arrowSizeWorld
    )
```

---

# 📐 8. Placement Decision Engine

This is critical.

---

# STEP 1 — Text Width

```pseudo id="g7jlwm"
textWidthPx =
    measureText(text)
```

---

# STEP 2 — Convert To World

```pseudo id="sqq2mh"
textWidthWorld =
    pixelsToWorld(
        textWidthPx
    )
```

---

# STEP 3 — Compare Against Diameter

```pseudo id="x9ucb3"
available =
    radius * 2
```

---

# STEP 4 — Fit Check

```pseudo id="4dffiv"
fitsInside =
    textWidthWorld <
    available * 0.75
```

---

# 🚀 Same principle as AutoCAD.

---

# 📐 9A. INSIDE Placement

---

# Text Position

```pseudo id="xjlwm3"
textPos = center
```

---

# Leader

```pseudo id="aprm3g"
leader =
    LINE(
        edgePoint,
        oppositePoint
    )
```

---

# Text Rotation

```pseudo id="7vjlwm"
rotation =
    normalizeReadable(
        ATAN2(v.y,v.x)
    )
```

---

# 📐 9B. OUTSIDE Placement

---

# Leader End

```pseudo id="xjlwm4"
leaderEnd =
    edgePoint
    + v * outsideOffset
```

---

# Text Position

```pseudo id="jlwm51"
textPos =
    leaderEnd
    + v * textGap
```

---

# Leader Geometry

```pseudo id="jlwm52"
leader1 =
    LINE(center, edgePoint)

leader2 =
    LINE(edgePoint, leaderEnd)
```

---

# 🚀 Classic CAD dog-leg leader.

---

# ⚡ 10. Optional Dogleg

---

# Horizontal Dogleg

```pseudo id="5jlwm5"
doglegEnd =
    leaderEnd + (doglegLength,0)
```

---

# Common in mechanical drawings.

---

# 📦 11. Final Render Data

```pseudo id="jlwm54"
RenderData {

  leaderLines[]

  arrowheads[]

  text

  textPosition

  textRotation
}
```

---

# 🧠 12. Important Production Rules

---

# A. Keep Text Upright

```pseudo id="jlwm55"
IF rotation upsideDown:
    rotation += 180°
```

---

# B. Small Circle

If radius too small:

```pseudo id="jlwm56"
forceOutsidePlacement()
```

---

# C. Zoom Stability

| Component | Space  |
| --------- | ------ |
| leader    | world  |
| arrow     | screen |
| text      | screen |

---

